    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0979" n="883" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg883"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Campbell to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port Louis, Mauritius</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 53.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The inclosed proclamations,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d750-f1"/> No. 10 and No. 11, were published on the dates affixed to
                    the newspaper clippings, inclosure No. 3. (April 23 and 26, respectively.)</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John P. Campbell</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d750-f1" n="2" xml:id="d750-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. The proclamation is in the same terms, mutatis mutandis, as that of
                    Great Britain, see <ref target="#pg865">page 865</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
